# Normalize line endings in the repository, then restore them on checkout.
#
# Everything is stored with LF. Windows contributors get LF too, so a clone
# produces byte-identical files regardless of who committed them. This matters
# here because Docker builds, SQL migrations and any script with a `#!` line all
# break or behave differently when CRLF leaks in.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native formats genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending filtered or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfiles are generated; keep diffs readable but still normalised.
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# Keep these out of language statistics and diffs: they are generated or large.
dashboard/data/** linguist-generated
*.db binary